    <h1>Whale season: a possible sighting</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">During certain months of the year it's possible to spot whales during the voyage to the Palomino Islands.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">Unlike sea lions and birds — which are guaranteed on every departure — whale sightings depend on the season and sea conditions, so we cannot guarantee them.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)">Based on records of whale watching along the Peruvian coast, the most likely window runs from <strong>July to October</strong> (with peak activity in August–September), when humpback whales migrate through the Pacific during their breeding season. Off Lima and Callao, sightings are occasional and depend on sea conditions.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3)"><strong>Sea lions and birds are guaranteed; whale sightings are a possibility and we cannot guarantee them.</strong></p>
